Both Loop Quantum Gravity and Causal Set Theory dismantle the classical picture of spacetime as a smooth, continuous backdrop—rebuilding it from the ground up using discrete, indivisible mathematical "atoms" of space and causality.
While we touched briefly on their core formulas earlier in E16, here is a deeper look at how each theory constructs 3D space, 4D time evolution, and Einstein's curved geometry out of pure discrete math.

1. Loop Quantum Gravity (LQG): Weaving Space from Quantum Loops

In Einstein’s General Relativity, gravity is the curvature of spacetime, and the metric field \(g_{\mu \nu }\) varies smoothly at every point. When Carlo Rovelli, Lee Smolin, and Abhay Ashtekar applied the rules of quantum mechanics directly to Einstein's equations (rewritten in Ashtekar variables, which treat gravity like a gauge field similar to electromagnetism), space itself fractured into discrete quanta.

A. How the "Atoms" Are Built: Holonomies & Spin Networks

Instead of measuring distances between points, LQG measures how quantum fields twist as you carry them around closed loops (called holonomies):
• Nodes (Quanta of Volume): Picture individual grains of space—each node is an indivisible chunk of 3D volume.
• Links (Quanta of Area): Adjacent nodes are connected by lines labeled with half-integer spin numbers \(j = \frac{1}{2}, 1, \frac{3}{2}, 2, \dots\) from the rotation group \(SU(2)\). Each link pierces the boundary between two grains of space, endowing that boundary with a discrete quantum of area:
\(A=8\pi \gamma \ell _{P}^{2}\sum _{i}\sqrt{j_{i}(j_{i}+1)}\)
(where \(\ell_P \approx 1.616 \times 10^{-35}\text{ m}\) is the Planck length and \(\gamma \) is the Barbero–Immirzi parameter).
• No "Empty" Space Between Nodes: Crucially, a spin network does not float inside a pre-existing empty room. The graph itself is space. Asking "what is between two nodes?" is meaningless—there is no space where there are no links.

B. How Time & Curvature Emerge: Spin Foams

A single spin network represents a frozen 3D snapshot of quantum space. To create 4D spacetime (time evolution):
• Nodes split and merge, and links reconnect in discrete quantum jumps—like frames in a movie.
• Tracing the history of a 2D spin network evolving through these local moves sweeps out a 2D combinatorial complex called a Spin Foam (where vertices represent discrete "ticks" of quantum time).
• When millions of spin-foam histories interfere quantum-mechanically (via a Feynman path integral), the large-scale average smoothly reproduces Einstein’s Field Equations—turning discrete combinatorial deficit angles around spin-foam faces into continuous spacetime curvature!

2. Causal Set Theory: "Order + Number = Geometry"

Proposed by Rafael Sorkin in 1987, Causal Set Theory takes an even more radical approach: instead of quantizing General Relativity, it strips spacetime down to pure cause-and-effect relationships and discrete counting.

A. The Two Fundamental Axioms

1. Causality (Partial Order): Reality is a set of elementary spacetime events \(C\) equipped with a binary relation \(\prec \) (where \(x \prec y\) means "event \(x\) can causally influence event \(y\)"):
	• Transitive: If \(x \prec y\) and \(y \prec z\), then \(x \prec z\).
	• Acyclic (No Time Travel): You cannot have both \(x \prec y\) and \(y \prec x\) for distinct events (forbidding closed timelike loops).
2. Discreteness (Local Finiteness): Between any two events \(x\) and \(y\), there is only a finite number of intermediate causal events—preventing spacetime from being infinitely divisible.

B. How Smooth 4D Spacetime Emerges: Poisson Sprinkling

How can a raw list of cause-and-effect arrows possibly look like smooth 4D Einsteinian spacetime?
• The Malament–Hawking Theorem: In General Relativity, knowing which events can send light signals to which other events (the causal light-cone structure) determines 90% of the metric geometry—every angle, shape, and curvature ratio—leaving only one missing ingredient: the local scale (volume).
• Counting Supplies Volume: In Causal Set Theory, each discrete event carries roughly one Planck 4-volume (\(\ell_P^4 \approx 10^{-140}\text{ m}^4\)). Counting the number of discrete atoms \(N\) inside a causal diamond gives its exact continuous spacetime volume \(V = N \cdot \ell_P^4\).
• Preserving Einstein’s Relativity Without a Grid: If you build space out of a rigid cubic crystal lattice, fast-moving observers see the grid contract differently in different directions, violating Einstein’s Special Relativity (Lorentz invariance). Causal Set Theory avoids this by placing events via a random Poisson sprinkling—creating a disordered network of causal links that looks statistically identical to observers moving at any speed!

